        "Text": {
          "text": "\n\n\n=== CURRENT ITERATION: 2 ===\n\n\n=== BOUND VARIABLES ===\n\nThese variables are already bound in lashlang. Access them directly in `<lashlang>` blocks; do not recreate them manually.\nSmall values are shown in full; larger ones show only a truncated preview (record keys, or the head and tail of a list/string) — but the variable still holds its COMPLETE value. A short preview never means state was lost; `print` the variable (or the part you need) to see the rest.\nNever write a field name you haven't seen in the key sets below — guessed field names silently produce zeros rather than errors. If a name is not listed, it does not exist on that value.\n\nAvailable variables:\n- `history`: `list[HistoryItem]`, read-only (descriptor: `list[any]`)\n\nSchema:\ntype HistoryItem =\n  | { kind: \"message\", id: str, role: enum[\"user\", \"system\", \"assistant\", \"event\"], content: str, attachments?: list[HistoryAttachment] }\n  | { kind: \"lashlang_step\", id: str, protocol_iteration: int, code: str, output: list[str], images?: list[HistoryImage], error?: str | null, final_output?: any | null }\ntype HistoryAttachment = { id: str, media_type?: str | null, label?: str | null, source: str, reference: str }\ntype HistoryImage = { id: str, media_type: str, width?: int | null, height?: int | null, bytes: int, label?: str | null }\n\nRuntime notes:\n- `history` currently has 1 entry\n\n\n=== FINALIZATION ===\n\nThis turn uses finish-required termination. Prose-only does not end the turn. Every non-terminal response must contain an `execute_code` call that performs the next step; prose before the code call is commentary/status only. Never say you will continue, inspect, patch, wait, monitor, validate, or retry unless the same response also contains the code call that does it. The terminal response must be an `execute_code` call that calls `finish <value>`. The value must match the REQUIRED OUTPUT contract.\n\n=== REQUIRED OUTPUT ===\n\nstr",
